# Project Architecture

Keep Presentation, Domain (if present), Data, and Core separate. This repo is feature-based. Match existing folders; do not rename `pages`/`widgets` to `views`/`components`.

```text
lib/features/<feature>/
  presentation/pages/
  presentation/widgets/
  cubit/
lib/core/          # theme, widgets, services, models, errors, helpers
```

Larger features may add `domain/` and `data/` only when the feature needs them. Do not add empty layers.

## Responsibilities

- **Pages:** Compose the screen and wire Bloc/Cubit. No business logic or I/O.
- **Widgets:** Independent UI sections. Constructor data in; no unnecessary app-state coupling.
- **Cubit/Bloc:** Feature state, business logic, loading/empty/error, calls to services.
- **Services:** APIs, Supabase, storage, and other I/O. Do not put navigation here.
- **Models:** Application data.
- **Core:** Shared utilities, extensions, constants, theme, common widgets.

Preferred flow: `Page → Cubit/Bloc → Service → API/DB`.

SOLID and separation of concerns apply. Prefer composition over inheritance. Do not introduce Provider, Riverpod, GetX, or ChangeNotifier for app state unless explicitly requested.
